            <ArticleTitle>Traumatic L4-L5 spondylolisthesis: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S232-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of L4-L5 traumatic anterolisthesis. The patient was treated surgically 4 months after the injury. His radiological and operative findings showed L4 inferior facet tip fracture, L4-L5 anterior displacement and left L4-L5 foraminal disc protrusion. Decompression, reduction with L3, L4, L5 pedicular screw fixation, L4-L5 disc excision and interbody cage insertion with autologous bone grafts were done. Flexion type injury was thought to be the probable mechanism.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
